SSIS Package Documentation – Master_ETL
🔹 1. Overview

This package is a Master ETL orchestration package that handles:

Full load for dimension/reference tables
Incremental load for transactional/domain tables
Batch control & execution tracking
Error handling and finalization

👉 In short:
It’s a production-style ETL pipeline with control tables and incremental logic (very strong for interviews).

🔹 2. High-Level Architecture
Main Components:
Full Load Section
Incremental Load Section
Finalization
Error Handling (On Failure)
🔹 3. Control Flow Breakdown
🧱 A. Full Load Sequence

SEQ_Full_Load_Tables

This handles static/reference tables using:

TRUNCATE → clear old data
DFT_* → reload data
Tables Loaded:
CustomerSegment
PaymentMethod
ProductCategory
ProductSubCategory
ShipmentType
Warehouse

👉 Pattern:

TRUNCATE TABLE → Data Flow Task (Reload Data)

✅ This is a full refresh strategy (good for small dimension tables)

🔄 B. Incremental Load Sequence

SEQ_Incremental_Load_Tables

This is the core part of your ETL 💥

It is divided into domains:

👤 1. Customer Domain

SEQ_Customer_Domain

Includes:
Customer
CustomerAddress
CustomerContact
CustomerLoginHistory
Pattern used (VERY IMPORTANT 🚨):

For each table:

Get LastSuccessfulLoad
Initialize Control Record (if not exists)
Mark as Running
Load Data (incremental)
Mark as Success
(Sometimes) Truncate staging

👉 This means you are using:

Control table / metadata-driven ETL
Incremental loading based on last load timestamp

💡 Interview insight:

This is a classic CDC (Change Data Capture)-like pattern without using native CDC

📦 2. Inventory Domain

SEQ_Inventory_Domain

Includes:
Inventory
InventoryMovement

Same pattern:

Last load tracking
Incremental extraction
Status updates
🔁 C. Common ETL Pattern Used

Across all incremental loads:

[Get Last Load]
      ↓
[Initialize if needed]
      ↓
[Mark as Running]
      ↓
[Load Data]
      ↓
[Mark as Success]

✅ This ensures:

Recoverability
Restartability
Audit tracking
🔚 D. Finalization

SEQ_Finalize_Package

Includes:

Close_Batch

👉 Likely used to:

Mark ETL batch as completed
Log execution end
❌ E. Error Handling

On Failure

Executes when the package fails
Used for:
Logging errors
Cleaning up
Marking batch as failed
